WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:08.149
Let's go to the phone lines at (617) 830-4750
and see what is on people's minds starting

00:00:08.149 --> 00:00:13.860
today with our caller from the two zero four
area code color from two zero four.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.860
What's your name?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.860
Where are you calling from?

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.860
Hi David.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.140
My name is Trevor.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:22.140
I'm calling from Winnipeg, Manitoba up in
Canada.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.949
Hey, how's it going today?

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:25.949
I'm doing pretty good.

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:28.060
Um, I just wanna pick your brain here.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:36.489
I was wondering why is it that Trump, um,
doesn't seem to attack Bernie as much as everybody

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:37.489
else?

00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:41.930
It seems, you know, there's so much, um, you
know, he used to talk about Biden and, and,

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:47.470
and um, Elizabeth Warren and just, but it
just seems like he doesn't, he doesn't push

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:53.210
the, the Bernie thing as much as, uh, as as
much as everybody else.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:55.040
Uh, do you find that too?

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.040
I do find that.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.600
I do think that he has this crazy Bernie nickname
and he's been tweeting about that.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.760
I think there's a couple of possibilities
here.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:06.549
One is he genuinely doesn't think Bernie is
going to be the nominee, so he feels it's

00:01:06.549 --> 00:01:08.220
a waste of time to talk about Bernie.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:14.140
The other possibility is he's actually scared
of having to go against Bernie in a way that

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:17.860
he's not scared of some of the others, although
it's mere speculation.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.680
I know that there's lots of hardcore Bernie
or busters who say, Bernie is the only guy

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.290
that could be Trump.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.439
So Trump is only afraid of Bernie.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.920
I've not seen any evidence of that.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.659
But it is possible that there's something
about Bernie that makes Trump hesitant to

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:37.390
attack them because of what he thinks might
happen if Bernie is indeed the nominee.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.350
But your guess is as good as mine.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:45.439
Yeah, I think, yeah, I kind of agree with
you that the I, I feel that the only reason

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:49.549
he hasn't really gone after him is, is he's
kind of scared of him.

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:52.350
You know what I, that's the only kind of thing
I could probably think of.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.350
You know,

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.920
the only thing is it doesn't really match
Trump's personality.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.342
Trump in general is not really scared of people
other than people who seem to kind of have

00:02:00.342 --> 00:02:01.342
them over a barrel.

00:02:01.342 --> 00:02:02.342
Right.

00:02:02.342 --> 00:02:05.850
Whether it's people who he owes money to or
people bailing him out financially, or whatever

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.179
the case, or people who have dirt on him.

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:10.389
I don't know that Bernie falls into those
categories.

00:02:10.389 --> 00:02:12.189
So it's, it would be unlike Trump.

00:02:12.189 --> 00:02:14.189
But again, we're just kind of speculating
here.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:20.730
My guess is if it seems clearer after a couple
of primaries that Bernie is a real contender

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:24.549
and starts to accumulate some delegates, my
guest is, you'll see Trump start to attack

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:26.420
him more.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.999
Yeah.

00:02:27.999 --> 00:02:28.999
To like that like, yeah.

00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:29.999
Yeah, exactly.

00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:33.459
Like it doesn't seem to be stared at anybody,
so that's why I was so kind of perplexed why

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:38.329
uh, he wouldn't be a full on attacking him
as much as everybody else.

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:39.329
Yeah.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:42.139
I mean three weeks from now we may be having
a different conversation depending on what

00:02:42.139 --> 00:02:43.139
happens.

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:44.189
Trevor, thank you for the call.

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:45.680
Yeah, thanks.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.760
I appreciate your show.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:47.760
Right.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:48.760
Great.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:48.765
Great to hear from you.

